{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-109089",
    "CVE-2026-109090",
    "CVE-2026-93542",
    "CVE-2026-93543"
  ],
  "description": "Adam Bedard discovered that libXi did not properly validate\nDEVICE_RESOLUTION replies from the X server, which could result in a heap\nbuffer overflow. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\napplications using libXi to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-109089)\n\nAdam Bedard discovered that libXi did not properly allocate memory when\nhandling DEVICE_ENABLE replies from the X server. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause applications using libXi to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-109090)\n\nIt was discovered that libXi did not properly validate class data in XI2\nreplies and events. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause applications using libXi to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-93542)\n\nIt was discovered that libXi did not properly validate class metadata in\nXI2 replies and events. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause applications using libXi to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-93543)",
  "id": "USN-9213-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in libXi.",
